<vertex eid="3"><attributes><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="type">entity</attribute><attribute class="com.flyinglogic.logicgraph.entityclass.EntityClass" key="entityClass"><entityClass name="Answered Yes" uuid="fa010909-0000-4000-8000-000000000002"/></attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="title">T01 [YES]
Short-window identity closed by amendment?</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">T01 | Short-window identity closed by amendment?

Status: YES

Method: Functional isolation / simulator

Scope / coordinates: I r-braincell-matched-027 against NEURON b1-fixed-027; 0.27 nA, copied x9 mesh, same dt 0.005 ms; window 270-329.5 ms.

Remaining search space: The amended recorded identity closure was met, or it was not; this is explicitly a recorded decision predicate.

Binary predicate: The basis reproduces the quoted values and identity_gate.closed is true under the recorded user amendment.

Decision limit: Amended basis: rise about 1.2e-9 ms, interpolated peak 5.4e-6 mV, width 1.9e-11 ms. Original 1e-6 mV automatic gate was not passed.

Recorded observation: identity_gate.closed=true by user decision; basis/passed=false under the stricter automatic gate. Both facts are retained.

YES: Keep the narrow closure; inspect the separate full-train predicate.

NO: Investigate matched simulator behavior within this window.

Next check: Read T02 for the full-train numerical prediction rather than extending this closure.

Unresolved after either answer: No inference to 0.19 nA, finer dt, H01 anatomy, or human waveform qualification.

Evidence (repository-relative):
docs/evidence/h01-i-transfer/sp2-close-decision.json
docs/evidence/h01-i-transfer-result.md

