<vertex eid="6"><attributes><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="type">entity</attribute><attribute class="com.flyinglogic.logicgraph.entityclass.EntityClass" key="entityClass"><entityClass name="Answered No" uuid="fa010909-0000-4000-8000-000000000003"/></attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="title">T02 [NO]
Strict full-train identity check passes?</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">T02 | Strict full-train identity check passes?

Status: NO

Method: Functional isolation / simulator

Scope / coordinates: I a1-matched-027 versus b1-fixed-027; same dt 0.005 ms and copied mesh; 270-1270 ms at 0.27 nA.

Remaining search space: All strict identity rows satisfy the registered prediction, or one or more do not.

Binary predicate: The full-train comparison has equal event counts and all strict per-event identity errors within the registered limits.

Decision limit: Rise 1e-8 ms, peak 1e-6 mV, width 1e-8 ms; retain sampled and interpolated peak definitions separately.

Recorded observation: 36/36 events; passed=false; max rise 1.415e-7 ms, raw voltage difference 8.33e-5 mV. Both sampled and interpolated peak errors exceed 1e-6 mV.

YES: Strict confirmation holds for this configuration.

NO: Retain the strict prediction failure without undoing or broadening T01's amended decision.

Next check: Before any rerun, reconcile sampled/interpolated peak fields with the scorer and document the failing strict rows. No tolerance relaxation.

Unresolved after either answer: Tiny simulator differences are not the millisecond fixed-step-vs-CVode drift, nor evidence of a human pass.

Evidence (repository-relative):
docs/evidence/h01-i-transfer/sp2-close-decision.json
docs/evidence/h01-i-transfer-result.md

