0.27 nA dt meets the crossing limit?</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">T03 | 0.27 nA dt meets the crossing limit?

Status: YES

Method: Hierarchical / numerical time

Scope / coordinates: NEURON finalist fixed dt 0.000625 ms versus CVode 1e-10, copied x9 mesh, 0.27 nA, 270-1270 ms.

Remaining search space: Equal event count and all rise errors &lt;=1 ms, or not.

Binary predicate: The fixed-step response has equal nonzero count and every paired rising-crossing error &lt;=1 ms.

Decision limit: 1 ms rise error and exact count for this timestep check only.

Recorded observation: 37/37 events; maximum rise error about 0.981 ms. This registered crossing check passes.

YES: Retain this measured timestep result for the stated input.

NO: Refine numerics before interpreting this crossing residual.

Next check: Evaluate the separate 0.19 nA result in T04; do not interpolate qualification across inputs.

Unresolved after either answer: This is not a complete mesh, peak, width or human validation verdict.

Evidence (repository-relative):
docs/evidence/h01-i-transfer/sp2-close-decision.json
docs/evidence/h01-i-transfer-result.md

