Anatomy swap alone changes the response?</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">T05 | Anatomy swap alone changes the response?

Status: OPEN

Method: Structural dissection / anatomy and region map

Scope / coordinates: Donor versus H01 morphology under frozen electrical controls and matched input, numerical, and measurement conventions; region map changes recorded separately.

Remaining search space: Qualified anatomy-only transfer contrast above the registered row limit versus no such contrast.

Binary predicate: A matched anatomy-only swap changes the selected response row beyond its established uncertainty.

Decision limit: Use per-row qualified numerical contrast limits, not donor physiological tolerance as a substitute for measurement resolution.

Recorded observation: Current H01 profiles include inferred electrical region assignments; unresolved Y1 concerns the upstream axonal outflow/region map.

YES: Dissect morphology/region boundaries carrying the contrast.

NO: Retain source-model/reference mismatch and other unsplit differences.

Next check: First enumerate anatomy and region-map differences; define one reversible matched swap with no invented cable and with both voltage and signed axial current.

Unresolved after either answer: Changing anatomy and region assignment together cannot identify which caused a contrast; donor data cannot directly validate H01 physiology.

